        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-o0ph8fryncjmw9u91va",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, meet your guide at the hotel at 08:00 for a two-hour sightseeing tour of Lake Atitlán.\n\nTravel along the shore by boat to an Indigenous village. You can also visit Santiago Atitlán and San Pedro. Your guide will tell you about the local communities and the traditions and customs they pass down from generation to generation.\n\nLake Atitlán lies in the crater of an extinct volcano. Tropical vegetation covers the crater’s basalt slopes, and you can see the surrounding mountains from the water. The nickname “Gringotenango” is also used here, with the gloss “space aliens”.\n\nThe town has few examples of colonial architecture, but it has a colourful market selling produce and local crafts.\n\nIn the afternoon, travel to Guatemala City.\n\nOvernight in Guatemala City at the Barceló hotel."
    },
